    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: KVM: arm64: vgic: Handle race between interrupt affinity change and LPI disabling (CVE-2026-72288)\n\n* kernel: KVM: arm64: vgic: Check the interrupt is still ours before migrating it (CVE-2026-72289)\n\n* kernel: scsi: target: iscsi: Reserve a terminator byte for the login payload (CVE-2026-90011)\n\n* kernel: KEYS: encrypted: fix integer overflow of datablob_len (CVE-2026-98222)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* ipv4: ip_gre: make ipgre_header() robust (rhel-8.10.z) (JIRA:RHEL-271135)\n\n* ip6_gre: make ip6gre_header() robust (rhel-8.10.z) (JIRA:RHEL-271136)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
